					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tygently" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2038009); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2038009&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467085" alt="TyGently" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2038009)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tygently" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2038009); return false;" >TyGently</a></span> <span class="odate time_1484704482 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Jan 2017 01:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2728700">
									

<p>This one's a very mixed bag, so I'm novoting for now. There were quite a few spelling errors and minor formatting issues, which I did my best to fix, feel free to roll it back if I made any changes in error.</p>
<p>Showing an alt-history can be fruitful, and you do some good things with it, but the migration from &quot;alt-history&quot; to &quot;Foundation-GOC war&quot; doesn't feel narratively natural, and the flashpoint being &quot;whoops the Foundation accidentally killed <em>three thousand gock agents</em>&quot; doesn't make a ton of sense.</p>
<p>Notable Good Bits:</p>
<ul>
<li>The picture is nice, compliments to Cyan.</li>
<li>The original timeline does paint a pretty interesting image of the world.</li>
<li>The Excerpts at the end are, in general, pretty well-written, and avoid narm for the most part. My favorite was the testimony from the Brazil resident.</li>
<li>The conclusion is relatively strong.</li>
</ul>
<p>Notable Bad Bits:</p>
<ul>
<li>Inclusion of 096 is a bit whack. Killing <em>six-figure numbers of civilians</em> is patently ridiculous, as well as off-handedly amnesticizing an entire country in five days.</li>
<li>Detaining over a thousand staff members over something obviously not from our timeline does not reflect well on the Foundation. It is very hard for a piece to be convincing when it makes the Foundation look incompetent.</li>
<li>The lack of information on what happens post-1946 or post-occult-war is a bit frustrating. Surely the Foundation could infer from the narration at least a few things about what the present is like in this world? For example, &quot;unlike x today&#8230;&quot;</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
					
